    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d513">

                <pb facs="1343" n="1327" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg1327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.31/1—1951: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Acting Chairman of the United States Delegation to the Torquay
                        Conference</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Corse</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d513-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-01-19T19:00:00-05:00">January 19, 1951—7
                            p. m</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>325. From State, Treas, Gomineree, Labor, EGA
                    and Agric. Re Deptel 316, Jan 15 and Deltels
                    354 and 355, Jan 17.</p>
                <p>1. Regret instrs refDeptel did not sufficiently emphasize view here US shld lend
                    strong active support to Blankenstein proposal, rather than qualified
                    concurrence reported Deltel 355.</p>
                <p>2. We are still of view every reasonable measure shld be taken make tangible
                    progress on Blakenstein proposal before Torquay adjournment. We are concerned
                    failure obtain results will lead to: (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) new
                    proposals for preferential low-tariff club in Eur; (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) stalemate in trade
                    liberalization program; (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) Benelux disaffection of Torquay negots and
                        GATT in gen.</p>
                <pb facs="1344" n="1328" xml:id="pg1328"/>
                <p>3. If extension longer than one week wld increase possibility positive results on
                    Blankenstein proposal, we request TAC reconsider
                    position reported Deltel 355 para 4a in order
                    recommend and support to CP’s longer
                    extension.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d513-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d513-f1-content">
